      This thesis is dedicated to the humanitarians of the Global South who carry the brunt of the labor without the deserved recognition or reward. 2024, the year I began the NOHA program, proved to be the deadliest year yet to be a humanitarian as 861 aid workers fell victim to attacks with 383 of those killed @aidworker2025. Not only were these humanitarians targeted while serving people in need, but also in their very own homes @UNPBS. It would be erasure not to point out the fact, verified by the United Nations, that more than half of these humanitarians were murdered in Gaza at the hands of Israeli forces @UNPBS. And so, to those humanitarians who do not have the privelege of flying in and out of a crisis, who are both witness and respondent to need, my thesis is in honor of you.
